{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\nusing u64 = unsigned long long;\n\nconstexpr u64 MAX_INT = (u64(1) << 63);\nu64 mod, n, k;\nvector<vector<u64>> table;\nvector<u64> fac, invfac;\n\nu64 mod_pow(u64 b, u64 e, u64 m) {\n    u64 res = 1;\n    b %= m;\n    while (e) {\n        if (e & 1) res = (res * b) % m;\n        b = (b * b) % m;\n        e >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nu64 nCr(int N, int R) {\n    if (R < 0 || R > N) return 0;\n    u64 res = fac[N];\n    res = (res * invfac[R]) % mod;\n    res = (res * invfac[N - R]) % mod;\n    return res;\n}\n\nu64 compute() {\n    u64 mx = max(n, k);\n    fac.assign(mx + 1, 0);\n    invfac.assign(mx + 1, 0);\n    fac[0] = 1;\n    for (u64 i = 1; i <= mx; ++i) fac[i] = (fac[i - 1] * i) % mod;\n    invfac[mx] = mod_pow(fac[mx], mod - 2, mod);\n    for (int i = mx - 1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        invfac[i] = (invfac[i + 1] * (i + 1)) % mod;\n    }\n    \n    int depth = min(18, (int)k);\n    table.assign(depth + 1, vector<u64>(300005, 0));\n    \n    for (u64 i = 1; i <= n; ++i) table[1][i] = invfac[i];\n    u64 result = (table[1][n] * nCr(k, 1)) % mod;\n    \n    for (int stage = 2; stage <= depth; ++stage) {\n        for (u64 mask = n; mask; mask = (mask - 1) & n) {\n            if (!table[stage - 1][mask]) continue;\n            u64 rest = n ^ mask;\n            for (u64 subset = rest; subset > mask; subset = (subset - 1) & rest) {\n                table[stage][mask ^ subset] += table[stage - 1][mask] * invfac[subset];\n                if (table[stage][mask ^ subset] > MAX_INT) table[stage][mask ^ subset] %= mod;\n            }\n        }\n        for (u64 mask = n; mask; mask = (mask - 1) & n) {\n            if (table[stage][mask] >= mod) table[stage][mask] %= mod;\n        }\n        u64 val = table[stage][n] * nCr(k, stage);\n        val %= mod;\n        val = (val * fac[stage]) % mod;\n        result += val;\n        if (result >= mod) result -= mod;\n    }\n    result = (result * fac[n]) % mod;\n    return result;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n >> k >> mod;\n    u64 res = mod_pow(k, n, mod);\n    if ((n & 1) == 0) {\n        res = (res - compute() + mod) % mod;\n    }\n    cout << res << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef mod_pow(b, e, m):\n    res = 1\n    b %= m\n    while e:\n        if e & 1:\n            res = (res * b) % m\n        b = (b * b) % m\n        e >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    mod = int(data[2])\n    \n    MAX_INT = 1 << 63\n    \n    # Precompute k^n mod mod\n    res = mod_pow(k, n, mod)\n    \n    # If n is odd, just output k^n mod mod\n    if n & 1:\n        print(res)\n        return\n    \n    # Compute the correction term using the compute() function logic\n    mx = max(n, k)\n    fac = [0] * (mx + 1)\n    invfac = [0] * (mx + 1)\n    fac[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, mx + 1):\n        fac[i] = (fac[i - 1] * i) % mod\n    \n    invfac[mx] = mod_pow(fac[mx], mod - 2, mod)\n    for i in range(mx - 1, -1, -1):\n        invfac[i] = (invfac[i + 1] * (i + 1)) % mod\n    \n    def nCr(N, R):\n        if R < 0 or R > N:\n            return 0\n        res = fac[N]\n        res = (res * invfac[R]) % mod\n        res = (res * invfac[N - R]) % mod\n        return res\n    \n    depth = min(18, k)\n    table = [[0] * 300005 for _ in range(depth + 1)]\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        table[1][i] = invfac[i]\n    \n    result = (table[1][n] * nCr(k, 1)) % mod\n    \n    for stage in range(2, depth + 1):\n        # Iterate over all masks that are subsets of n\n        mask = n\n        while mask:\n            if table[stage - 1][mask]:\n                rest = n ^ mask\n                subset = rest\n                while subset > mask:\n                    table[stage][mask ^ subset] += table[stage - 1][mask] * invfac[subset]\n                    if table[stage][mask ^ subset] > MAX_INT:\n                        table[stage][mask ^ subset] %= mod\n                    subset = (subset - 1) & rest\n            mask = (mask - 1) & n\n        \n        # Modulo reduction for this stage\n        for mask in range(n + 1):\n            if table[stage][mask] >= mod:\n                table[stage][mask] %= mod\n        \n        val = table[stage][n] * nCr(k, stage)\n        val %= mod\n        val = (val * fac[stage]) % mod\n        result += val\n        if result >= mod:\n            result -= mod\n    \n    result = (result * fac[n]) % mod\n    res = (res - result + mod) % mod\n    print(res)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00020251607929822057, -7.152555099310121e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.04431784525513649, -6.90197994117625e-05, -0.0036379601806402206, -0.07290493696928024, -0.0820339024066925, -3.0993935070000